# appease — success
#
# Gentling a hostile beast out of hostility. Forced past the dice.
#
# --spawn-beast is what makes this reachable: appease only applies to an ENEMY (or an annoying
# acquaintance), and a wilderness factory rolls a beast 10–40% of the time and then lets it roam.
# The spawned one is flagged an enemy by the same first-contact pass that flags a rolled one.
#
# This used to exist only as the first half of cli/tame/success.cli — a beast that still wants to
# kill you cannot be tamed, so taming is appease-then-tame. Split out so the verb has its own test.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon --observe-only wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect wolf

strategy succeed
goal appease
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect SUCCESS

# What makes this an appease test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb appease
quit
